            <h3><strong>Deposit Result Callback Method</strong></h3>
            <p>
                This documentation describes how to handle callback requests sent by the <span class="text-danger">sendDepositResultCallback</span> function in your service.
            </p>

            <p><strong>Method: </strong><span class="text-danger">POST</span></p>

            <p><strong>Deposit Result Callback Endpoint : </strong> <span class="text-danger">{PARTNER_SITE_ENDPOINT}</span></p>

            <table class="table table-bordered">
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Parameter</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>Type</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>Description</strong></td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>userID</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>User's ID in the site</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>username</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>User's username</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>name</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>User's name</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>amount</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>Numeric</td>
                        <td>Transaction amount</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>verifiedAmount</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>Numeric</td>
                        <td>Verified transaction amount</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>transaction_id</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>Unique transaction ID</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>status</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>Integer</td>
                        <td>Transaction status (e.g., 1: Pending 2: Approved 3: Rejected)</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>type</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>Transaction type ('Deposit')</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>payment_method_id</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>Payment method ID used in the transaction</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>
                            <p>hash</p>
                        </td>
                        <td>String</td>
                        <td>SHA1 hash for transaction validation</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

            <h5>Validating the Transaction</h5>
            <p>
                To validate the request, calculate the <span class="text-danger">hash</span> using the following formula and compare it with the received
            </p>
            <pre>
                <code>
    hash = sha1(transaction_id + userID + status + type)
                </code>
            </pre>

            <p>
                If the calculated hash does not match the received one, the request should not be processed.
            </p>
            <h5>Response</h5>
            <p>
                Upon successful completion of the callback processing, your system should return a response in the following JSON format:
            </p>
            <pre>
                <code>
    {
        "success": true,
        "message": "The process was completed successfully"
    }
                </code>
            </pre>

